  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> be a complex number with non-zero imaginary part. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is a real number, then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "0.5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>z</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>z</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>z</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mrow><msup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp; (given)</p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>",
